    "body": "## Problem and source changes\n\nThe previous integrated source produced real native failures and incomplete qualification. This draft preserves those results while applying the reviewed repairs and diagnostics needed for the next exact-source run.\n\nCurrent source head: `9bd2f589debdba4a93baa363817c3669cb103721`; tree: `c77785ecb368c44ea699769001a47402c9f50591`.\n\nThe source contains 103 cumulative changed paths against `2ae5215beaf8d7b7df111a090b82134beae2683d`, including the earlier owner/custody changes and:\n\n- Fresh-owner qualification lease clocks, with ordinary production clocks, expiry checks and original test budgets preserved.\n- Model-list wire/cache and remote-control fixture corrections; bounded failure-stage diagnostics for startup, Matrix, neuron and plugin-cache paths.\n- The pinned Nextest JUnit workspace location.\n- Same-handle, before-truncation hardlink checks for the typed Windows restricted filesystem writer, with unrestricted behavior preserved.\n- Explicit retirement of the durable-holdout file lock and retained-handle coverage.\n- Twenty-one reviewed formatter changes from the exact source-only operation.\n\nThe Windows ordinary-host delete diagnostics do not repair the separate elevated outside-root deletion failure. No partial permission-policy rewrite or disabled-feature result is presented as recovered capability.\n\n## Completed validation\n\n- [Source-only run 43015979473](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/hepta-private-ci/actions/runs/43015979473), job 130507034042: the original 600-second operation completed in 393.996016 seconds. All 103 input/output paths and three complete Git trees were verified; 13 old case names had zero hits; caller verification covered 6,200 Rust files with authorityGranted=false. The resulting formatter tree above was independently reviewed before materialization as this source commit.\n- [Exact-source Bazel lock run 43020939762](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/hepta-private-ci/actions/runs/43020939762), job 130523679401: one actual `just bazel-lock-update`, 26.462319 seconds within the original 1,200-second command budget, exit 0, no timeout or output overflow. Exact source and both Cargo/Bazel lock files remained clean and byte-identical before/after. Original module/annotation warnings remain in the raw log.\n- Full original ZIPs, raw receipts and source identities were independently audited. The earlier zero-job source workflow failure and the Bazel version-probe failure remain separate original records.\n\n## Native qualification and adoption\n\nThis ref update admits the new source to its ordinary full native CI. Results on old `189711` are not passes on this source, and source/lock checks do not establish Rust compilation, Windows isolation, actual retained-memory benefit, or owner recovery.\n\nThe previous blocking run had 23 successful, 10 failed and 4 skipped jobs. Original Windows-current ended with 137 PASS, one LEAK and one FAIL among 139 observed cases, with 28 expected cases lacking terminals. The elevated outside-delete assertion and the separate Bazel ordinary-host failure remain distinct.\n\nAll ten adoption gates remain open. Existing provider UNKNOWN state, independent trust/exposure requirements, original budgets, assertions and thresholds are preserved. No new real model generation, different-key provider replay or Provider G execution is authorized by this PR update.\n\nEvidence and owner ledgers remain in draft PRs [#5889](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/hepta-private-ci/pull/5889) and [#5897](https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/hepta-private-ci/pull/5897). No merge or deployment is performed.",
